what: `Schema.Step` — the depth-aware value walk written once — and
  the value algebras moved onto `fold` + `Step`: `Json.encode`,
  `Cbor.put`, `Form.render`, `Form.errorsOf`; their hand-rolled `*C`
  twins deleted. JMH bar (CodecBenchmark, uptime first, >=3 forks):
  no interpreted encode lane worse by more than its own error bar;
  the staged doors untouched and identical. The open design question
  the spec left to measurement: a fold is per SCHEMA, an encode call
  is per VALUE — where the folded interpreter is cached, and what that
  costs on the hot path, is this lane's finding.
